Rob here with a GS news update Microsoft  has admitted that rise of the Tomb  Raider will not be an Xbox exclusive  forever it was announced during  Microsoft's event at Gamescom yesterday  that rise of the Tomb Raider would be an  Xbox exclusive for holiday 2015 angering  many fans of the series but the wording  of the announcement was misleading  causing many to assume the game would be  an Xbox exclusive title for ever coming  holiday 2015 exclusively to xbox Xbox  boss Phil Spencer has admitted that the  exclusivity deal won't last forever when  asked if there is a limited period of  time covered by the deal Spencer replied  yes the deal has a duration I didn't buy  it I don't own the franchise so the game  is still exclusive to Xbox platforms but  only during holiday 2015 sometime after  that it will come to other platforms  perhaps exclusive wasn't quite the right  word for this arrangement the release  date of the game is still unknown it is  coming to xbox one and on xbox 360 at  the end of 2015 and it can be assumed  that PlayStation 3 4 and pc will get the  game at some later date what's your  opinion of the whole situation do you  feel better now that xbox has admitted  that it won't be just theirs or do you  feel that they could have worded the  whole thing a little bit better leave  your comment in section below have a  great day see you later  you
 

